  "tours": [
    {
      "id": "tour:parse-errors",
      "title": "How Zod parse and safeParse handle invalid input",
      "summary": "A caller picks `safeParse` to branch on a result flag instead of catching an error. In synchronous classic Zod, both methods run the schema and inspect its issues. On invalid input, `parse` throws an error. `safeParse` returns a failed result that builds its error only when read. Either method throws an async error if the schema unexpectedly returns a Promise.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:1"
          ],
          "note": "### Choose the synchronous classic method\n\n`parse` throws on validation issues. `safeParse` returns a result whose `success` flag tells the caller whether validation passed.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/classic/schemas.ts",
              "find": "return parse.parse(this, data, params, { callee: _parse });",
              "role": "call-site"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/classic/schemas.ts",
              "find": "return parse.safeParse(this, data, params);",
              "role": "call-site"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/classic/schemas.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t2",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:2",
            "outcome:8"
          ],
          "note": "### Both methods run the schema\n\nEach method calls the synchronous schema run with an empty issue list. If that run unexpectedly returns a Promise, either method throws an async error.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parse",
              "find": "const result = schema._zod.run({ value, issues: [] }, ctx);",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_safeParse",
              "find": "const result = schema._zod.run({ value, issues: [] }, ctx);",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t3",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:3"
          ],
          "note": "### No issues return parsed data\n\nThe caller of parse gets the value with no wrapper. safeParse wraps it as `{ success: true, data }`, so the caller tests the success flag before it reads the data.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parse",
              "find": "return result.value as core.output<typeof schema>;",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_safeParse",
              "find": "({ success: true, data: result.value } as any)",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t4",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:5",
            "outcome:4"
          ],
          "note": "### Issues produce different outcomes\n\nparse throws an error that holds the finished issues, so the caller needs a try block. safeParse returns `{ success: false, error }` from `failure`, so the caller branches on the success flag.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parse",
              "find": "throw e;",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_safeParse",
              "find": "failure(_Err, result.issues, ctx)",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t5",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:4",
            "outcome:6",
            "outcome:7"
          ],
          "note": "### The failed result constructs its error on demand\n\nA caller that needs only the flag avoids the cost of finalizing issues. Reading the error later pays that cost once.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "failure",
              "find": "get error() {",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "failure",
              "find": "error = new Err(issues.map((iss) => util.finalizeIssue(iss, ctx, core.config())));",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-next",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:1"
          ],
          "note": "### Where to go next\n\n`parseAsync` and `safeParseAsync` return the same two shapes for a schema with async checks; the caller awaits them. `util.finalizeIssue` picks the message of each issue that the error holds.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parseAsync",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/util.ts",
              "symbol": "finalizeIssue",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
